            <ArticleTitle>External nasal nerve division: a treatment for post-traumatic neuralgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>915-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present four patients complaining of neuralgic pains across the nasal bridge following trauma, who were successfully treated by division of the external nasal nerve. We believe it is a useful treatment in selected cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
